🚽 Test case: #206 (3e) -- indexing into an array field reached through a
🚽 chain of nested-struct member access (`o.inner.vals[i]`), not just a
🚽 direct field. Array.base (ast.h) holds the whole struct_access
🚽 expression, and struct_access already resolves chains of any depth on
🚽 its own (resolve_struct_access() recurses when the object is itself a
🚽 NODE_STRUCT_ACCESS), so this should fall out for free with no extra
🚽 chain-specific code.
gang Inner {
    rizz vals[3];
};
gang Outer {
    gang Inner inner;
};

skibidi main {
    gang Outer o;
    o.inner.vals[0] = 10;
    o.inner.vals[1] = 20;
    o.inner.vals[2] = 30;
    yapping("%d %d %d", o.inner.vals[0], o.inner.vals[1], o.inner.vals[2]);
}
